308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I like this a lot! All these templates were way overdue for a simplification. I think you did a great job on this PR.\r\n\r\nIt's difficult to be _completely_ sure that everything works as expected - but the biggest hurdle with templates is getting it to compile. I've spotted no mistakes with the logic beyond that.\r\n\r\nThe biggest risk I see with more templating vs explicit declaratinos is that you can accidentally overgeneralize and match types you don't want to match. I've raised the boolean problem before, and there may be others like it (although I didn't immediately spot any). Before merging, please make doubly sure that each declaration is as airtight as it can be.","state":"APPROVED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101003#pullrequestreview-2744966727","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101003","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101003#pullrequestreview-2744966727"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101003"}},"submitted_at":"2025-04-05T19